> **Summary:** This is the authoritative legend for contact reason categorization used across financial reporting, product improvement tracking, and operational reporting. Reference this any time you are unsure how to tag a ticket's Type or Interaction Subject in Airtable.

---

## Why Categorization Matters

Accurate contact reason tagging feeds:
- Financial reporting
- Product improvement decisions
- Operational improvement decisions
- Product and operational issue rate and cost tracking

If you are unsure how to categorize an interaction, reach out to your CH Lead or the CH Division Owner.

---

## Contact Reason Reference Table

### Product Issues

| Interaction Subject | Definition | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Defective** | All parts are fully intact but the product **cannot be correctly assembled** due to being improperly manufactured. | Pre-drilled holes too big, too small, stripped, missing, misaligned, or in wrong place; improperly or incorrectly welded; parts too big, too small, or misaligned; parts bent or warped; missing minor parts not on IS list that prevent assembly (e.g. missing a pre-installed insert for a bolt) |
| **Unstable** | The product **can be assembled** but is not sturdy when fully tightened and assembled correctly. Parts are not defective and not broken. | Off-balance; wiggles or wobbles; unstable; shaky |
| **Broken Parts** | The product **cannot be assembled** OR is **not safe to use** because a part is broken or severely damaged. | Broken doors, shelves, footrests, legs, stretcher, leaf, frame, etc. Significant wood splinters posing a safety risk. |
| **Damaged in Transit** | The product arrived with the outer box significantly damaged, which appears to have contributed to product damage or missing parts, as confirmed by images or customer description. | "Box looked destroyed when it arrived so I've attributed those issues to that."; "Large hole in the box and I believe the hardware fell out."; "Box arrived soaking wet and materials were damaged." |
| **Finishing > Surface Imperfections** | Product can be assembled, is safe to use, and functions as intended, but there is a minor manufacturing defect, damage, or other issue on the surface of part(s). | Scratches, chips, gouges, dents; discoloration or stains; uneven stain application; misaligned nail heads; peeling finish or bubbling laminate; air bubbles in glass shades; noticeable sheen differences within the same unit; damage to cushions (rips, foam damage, dents, excessive wrinkles) |
| **Finishing > Bubbling/Fraying Rattan or Textilene** | Product can be assembled and functions as intended, but rattan or textilene is lifting, bubbling, or visibly fraying (even if fraying is considered normal/expected). | Customer concerned about rattan fraying present on the unit |
| **Finishing > Color Mismatch Between Units** | Product can be assembled and functions as intended, but there are aesthetic flaws or color inconsistencies between multiple units or parts of the same SKU. | One unit is visibly lighter/darker than another of the same SKU; finish tone varies significantly between components of the same item |
| **Missing / Wrong / Broken Hardware** | Product **cannot be assembled** due to missing, wrong, or physically broken hardware. The issue can be resolved by sending a replacement hardware pack. Indicate the type (missing, wrong, or broken) in the notes. | No hardware in the box; one or more hardware pieces missing; hardware is not correct for assembling the unit |
| **Missing Part** | Product **cannot be fully assembled** because a part is missing (including missing inserts). The product is **not** defective. | Part A was not included in the package |
| **Wrong Part** | Customer received all parts but they are incorrect; product cannot be assembled as a result. | Customer received 2x Part A but should have received 1x Part A and 1x Part B |
| **Missing Instructions** | A physical copy of the instructions was not included in the box. **Note:** Not the same as "I lost the instructions." Sending virtual instructions when a customer lost the physical version is categorized under **Product Question**. | Instructions not in box upon opening |

