### Order Issues

| Interaction Subject | Definition | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Rec. Duplicate** | Customer received a duplicate item — too many of the same product. In the QTY field, indicate the number of extra units received. In comments, note how it was resolved (keeping or returning). | Ordered 2 Hylie Stools, received 3. QTY = 1; Notes = Customer is keeping the duplicate stool |
| **Rec. Wrong Item** | The wrong product was shipped. The product received is different from what was ordered. | Customer orders 32704 but receives 32701; customer orders 45001 but receives 32202 |
| **Did Not Receive** | Tracking shows delivered but customer says they never received the item. | Tracking shows delivered but customer claims it never arrived (lost, wrong address, or stolen); tracking was never generated (not shipped) |
| **Lost in Transit** | Customer never received the item and tracking does not indicate delivery. OR tracking was never generated and order is unfulfilled. | Tracking generated but no movement after 14 days; tracking showed some movement but order did not deliver and movement stopped |

