### Non-Guarantee Issues

| Interaction Subject | Definition | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Normal Wear and Tear** | Customer reports damage that is a result of wear and tear over use and/or time. | Laminate cracking/peeling after 100+ days; table-top developed scratches over time |
| **Damaged During Assembly** | Customer damaged the unit during assembly and cannot reassemble it correctly as a result. | Cam bolts tightened too much and punctured top panel; back panel assembled upside-down and damaged while removing; holes stripped with power tools |
| **Lost Hardware** | Customer lost the hardware or was not supplied hardware upon being gifted a used item. | Moved and lost hardware; needs replacement template to reinstall headboard; gifted item used and missing unique hardware |
| **Damage from Cleaning/Misuse/Modification** | Customer damaged the item via improper cleaning, improper use, commercial use, or modification attempt. | Burned bookcase shelves with a candle; damaged item while cleaning; commercial use damage; attempted to stain wood furniture and damaged finish; shelf warped from overloading |

