### Sales Issues

| Interaction Subject | Definition | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Advertising/PDP Error** | Nathan James made an explicit error on our PDPs, our retailers' PDPs, or in advertising materials. **Special case:** Customer feels we misrepresented materials (e.g. "Solid Wood" in title when item isn't fully solid wood; customer expected solid faux marble but received marble paper laminate) — count as Advertising Issue to inform future PDP decisions. | Incorrect dimensions listed on PDP; bedroom set contained mix of natural and faux rattan when customer expected a match; PDP photos showed a feature (e.g. cord management hole) never released for that SKU; received a version of an item (e.g. flat-packed vs assembled) that doesn't match the PDP |
| **OOS** | Unable to fulfill an order because the item(s) are out of stock. | |
| **Pre-Purchase Price Inquiry > Match Shopify Price** | A Shopify customer requests a price match on a product they plan to purchase. | "Can you match the price I paid for my first stool?"; "I missed the Memorial Day sale by one day, can you match yesterday's price?" |
| **Pre-Purchase Price Inquiry > Match Retailer Price** | Customer requests a price match on a product they see cheaper at another retailer. **(These price matches are not covered by our policy.)** | "Amazon has it for $30 cheaper — can you match the price?" |
| **Post-Purchase Price Inquiry > Adjust to Shopify Price** | A Shopify customer requests a price adjustment on a product they already purchased. | "I purchased your Theo Bookcase 2 days ago and today the price is $10 cheaper. Can you refund the difference?" |
| **Post-Purchase Price Inquiry > Adjust to Retailer Price** | A Shopify customer requests a price adjustment for a retailer sale after purchasing from our website. | "I purchased from you last week but Amazon now has it cheaper — can you match or accept a return?" |

