### Feedback

| Interaction Subject | Definition | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **Assembly Confusion** | Customer struggled to assemble the item or reported a "product issue" that was actually assembly confusion, but **did not damage the item in the process.** | "My Mina Side Table has defective hinges!" (hinges installed incorrectly); "The holes in my Linus Bar Stool legs are drilled in the wrong spots!" (customer swapped front legs) |
| **Persistent Odor/Smell** | Item has a persistent smell that doesn't dissipate significantly after 1–2 weeks. | |
| **General Feedback** | Positive or negative feedback about the product where there is no clear product, order, or sales issue. | "The assembly process was so easy!"; "The bookcase looks so great in my office!"; "The quality of the materials was incredibly deficient for the price I paid" |
| **Product Requests/Suggestions** | Customer shares a suggestion about an existing or non-existing product, with no product, order, or sales issue involved. **Note: If an issue is involved, categorize the issue separately.** | "Would you ever make a headboard in the Enloe herringbone style?"; "Can you make the Theo 6-shelf with the dimensions of the Theo 5-shelf?" |

